theory.intro:
The **displacement** from one position to another is the vector $\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{2})-\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{1})$. It points from the first position to the second. Its magnitude is the distance between the two positions.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0)--(6.4,0) node[right,font=\footnotesize] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,4.6) node[above,font=\footnotesize] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.6:5.8,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.3*\x*\x-2.0*\x+4.6});
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (1.2,2.632);
\coordinate (Q) at (5.2,2.312);
\draw[->,gray] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left,font=\footnotesize] {$\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{1})$};
\draw[->,gray] (O)--(Q) node[midway,below right,font=\footnotesize] {$\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{2})$};
\draw[->,very thick,red] (P)--(Q) node[midway,above,font=\footnotesize] {$\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{2})-\underset{\sim}{r}(t_{1})$};
\fill (P) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.2pt);
\node[below left,font=\footnotesize] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
$\underset{\sim}{r}(0)=5\underset{\sim}{i}$
$\underset{\sim}{r}(3)=2\underset{\sim}{i}+3\underset{\sim}{j}$
$\underset{\sim}{r}(3)-\underset{\sim}{r}(0)=(2-5)\underset{\sim}{i}+(3-0)\underset{\sim}{j}$
$=-3\underset{\sim}{i}+3\underset{\sim}{j}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0)--(6.4,0) node[right,font=\footnotesize] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8)--(0,4.6) node[above,font=\footnotesize] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=2:5,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x-8*\x+15});
\coordinate (A) at (5,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3);
\draw[->,very thick,red] (A)--(B) node[midway,above right,font=\footnotesize] {$-3\underset{\sim}{i}+3\underset{\sim}{j}$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[below right,font=\footnotesize] {$t=0$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above left,font=\footnotesize] {$t=3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
